---- MODULE PrimaryBackup_MC ----
\* Model-checking wrapper for the relational PrimaryBackup spec generated by verus2tla.
\* Adds message channel, VARIABLE state, finite domains, and safety invariants.
\*
\* The generated spec uses relational-style (s, s_, c) parameters with sent_packets
\* output. This wrapper adds explicit message tracking to enable TLC model checking.
\*
\* The wrapper adds protocol phase tracking (Idle/WaitBackup/WaitAck/ReadyToCommit)
\* to enforce the correct write-replicate-ack-commit ordering on top of the
\* set-based asynchronous message channel.

EXTENDS Integers, Sequences, FiniteSets

\* Finite model constants for TLC
CONSTANTS Primary_tag, Inactive_tag

\* Finite value domain for model checking
Values == {0, 1, 2}
MaxLogLen == 3
MaxView == 2

\* State variables
VARIABLE state, constants, msgs

\* Construct the constants record
ConstantsRecord == [max_log_len |-> MaxLogLen]

\* Role tags (modeled as tagged records matching generated spec's s.role.tag usage)
PrimaryRole == [tag |-> Primary_tag]
InactiveRole == [tag |-> Inactive_tag]

\* Protocol phases for write cycle
\* "Idle"          - no pending write, ready to accept new writes
\* "WaitBackup"    - replicate sent, waiting for backup to receive
\* "WaitAck"       - backup received, ack sent, waiting for primary to receive ack
\* "ReadyToCommit" - ack received, ready to commit

\* Message types
ReplicateMsg(v) == [type |-> "Replicate", val |-> v]
AckMsg == [type |-> "Ack"]

\* --- Protocol actions (adapted from generated Primarybackup.tla with message tracking) ---

\* Primary writes a new value (client request)
PrimaryWrite(val) ==
    /\ state.role = PrimaryRole
    /\ state.phase = "Idle"
    /\ state.has_pending = FALSE
    /\ state.log_length < ConstantsRecord.max_log_len
    /\ val \in Values
    /\ state' = [state EXCEPT !.has_pending = TRUE,
                               !.pending_value = val,
                               !.acked = FALSE]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<msgs, constants>>

\* Primary sends replicate message to backup
PrimarySendReplicate ==
    /\ state.role = PrimaryRole
    /\ state.has_pending = TRUE
    /\ state.acked = FALSE
    /\ state.phase = "Idle"
    /\ state' = [state EXCEPT !.phase = "WaitBackup"]
    /\ msgs' = msgs \cup {ReplicateMsg(state.pending_value)}
    /\ UNCHANGED constants

\* Backup receives replicate message and applies it
BackupReceiveReplicate(val) ==
    /\ state.role = PrimaryRole
    /\ state.phase = "WaitBackup"
    /\ ReplicateMsg(val) \in msgs
    /\ state' = [state EXCEPT !.backup_log_length = state.backup_log_length + 1,
                               !.backup_last_value = val,
                               !.backup_synced = TRUE,
                               !.phase = "WaitAck"]
    /\ msgs' = msgs \ {ReplicateMsg(val)}
    /\ UNCHANGED constants

\* Backup sends ack to primary
BackupSendAck ==
    /\ state.role = PrimaryRole
    /\ state.phase = "WaitAck"
    /\ state.backup_synced = TRUE
    /\ state' = [state EXCEPT !.phase = "ReadyToCommit"]
    /\ msgs' = msgs \cup {AckMsg}
    /\ UNCHANGED constants

\* Primary receives ack from backup
PrimaryReceiveAck ==
    /\ state.role = PrimaryRole
    /\ state.phase = "ReadyToCommit"
    /\ state.has_pending = TRUE
    /\ AckMsg \in msgs
    /\ state' = [state EXCEPT !.acked = TRUE,
                               !.phase = "ReadyToCommit"]
    /\ msgs' = msgs \ {AckMsg}
    /\ UNCHANGED constants

\* Primary commits the pending write
PrimaryCommit ==
    /\ state.role = PrimaryRole
    /\ state.acked = TRUE
    /\ state.has_pending = TRUE
    /\ state' = [state EXCEPT !.log_length = state.log_length + 1,
                               !.last_value = state.pending_value,
                               !.has_pending = FALSE,
                               !.pending_value = 0,
                               !.acked = TRUE,
                               !.phase = "Idle"]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<msgs, constants>>

\* Primary fails (crashes) -- can happen at any time when Primary
PrimaryFail ==
    /\ state.role = PrimaryRole
    /\ state' = [state EXCEPT !.role = InactiveRole,
                               !.has_pending = FALSE,
                               !.pending_value = 0,
                               !.acked = TRUE,
                               !.backup_synced = FALSE,
                               !.phase = "Idle"]
    /\ msgs' = {}  \* clear in-flight messages on failure
    /\ UNCHANGED constants

\* Backup promotes to primary (failover)
BackupPromote ==
    /\ state.role = InactiveRole
    /\ state.view < MaxView  \* bound view for finite model checking
    /\ state' = [state EXCEPT !.role = PrimaryRole,
                               !.log_length = state.backup_log_length,
                               !.last_value = state.backup_last_value,
                               !.has_pending = FALSE,
                               !.pending_value = 0,
                               !.acked = TRUE,
                               !.backup_synced = TRUE,
                               !.view = state.view + 1,
                               !.phase = "Idle"]
    /\ msgs' = {}  \* clear stale messages on failover
    /\ UNCHANGED constants

\* --- Standard TLA+ state machine ---

StateInit ==
    /\ constants = ConstantsRecord
    /\ state = [role |-> PrimaryRole,
                log_length |-> 0,
                last_value |-> 0,
                has_pending |-> FALSE,
                pending_value |-> 0,
                acked |-> TRUE,
                backup_log_length |-> 0,
                backup_last_value |-> 0,
                backup_synced |-> TRUE,
                view |-> 0,
                phase |-> "Idle"]
    /\ msgs = {}

StateNext ==
    \/ \E val \in Values : PrimaryWrite(val)
    \/ PrimarySendReplicate
    \/ \E val \in Values : BackupReceiveReplicate(val)
    \/ BackupSendAck
    \/ PrimaryReceiveAck
    \/ PrimaryCommit
    \/ PrimaryFail
    \/ BackupPromote

vars == <<state, constants, msgs>>

Spec == StateInit /\ [][StateNext]_vars

\* --- Safety Invariants ---

\* Log consistency: after a full write-replicate-ack-commit cycle, backup log >= primary log
\* When the primary is idle (acked, no pending), backup has replicated everything committed
LogConsistencyAfterAck ==
    (state.role = PrimaryRole /\ state.acked = TRUE /\ state.has_pending = FALSE) =>
        state.backup_log_length >= state.log_length

\* No split brain: role is always one of the two valid states
NoSplitBrain ==
    state.role = PrimaryRole \/ state.role = InactiveRole

\* Log lengths are bounded by the finite domain
LogLengthBound ==
    /\ state.log_length <= MaxLogLen
    /\ state.backup_log_length <= MaxLogLen

\* View monotonicity: view is always non-negative and bounded
ViewBounded ==
    /\ state.view >= 0
    /\ state.view <= MaxView

\* Backup coherence: when synced and idle, backup has at least as much as primary
BackupLogCoherence ==
    (state.role = PrimaryRole /\ state.backup_synced = TRUE /\ state.has_pending = FALSE /\ state.acked = TRUE) =>
        state.backup_log_length >= state.log_length

\* If has_pending, the system must be in Primary role (only primary accepts writes)
PendingImpliesValidState ==
    state.has_pending = TRUE => state.role = PrimaryRole

====
